1
00:00:01,450 --> 00:00:11,950
Jesus once told a story. There was a father who had two sons. The big brother worked in the field every day. The little brother... just liked to play.

2
00:00:13,950 --> 00:00:19,480
Dad! Give me my share of everything now. I want to go far away and have some fun!

3
00:00:20,380 --> 00:00:26,610
Oh... all right, my son. Here it is. Please... be careful.

4
00:00:30,240 --> 00:00:32,810
Bye-bye! I'm off to live the good life!

5
00:00:34,610 --> 00:00:37,290
Hmph. All he thinks about is having fun.

6
00:00:39,990 --> 00:00:47,250
In the far country he threw parties every day, bought sweets and fancy clothes, and spent money like water.

7
00:00:47,650 --> 00:00:51,010
Eat whatever you like, everyone! It's on me!

8
00:00:51,210 --> 00:00:53,630
Yay! You're the best!

9
00:00:56,330 --> 00:00:59,510
Huh? Where's my money?... There's none left?

10
00:01:00,010 --> 00:01:04,530
No money? Oh... well, we're off then. Bye!

11
00:01:07,190 --> 00:01:12,090
And just then a great famine came to that land. There was nothing to eat.

12
00:01:14,220 --> 00:01:16,540
So he had to take a job feeding pigs.

13
00:01:20,140 --> 00:01:24,160
I'm so hungry... even the pigs' pods look yummy...

14
00:01:27,060 --> 00:01:33,130
Even the workers at my dad's house have plenty to eat... and here I am, starving.

15
00:01:35,370 --> 00:01:37,170
That's it! I'll go home!

16
00:01:38,170 --> 00:01:46,890
Dad, I was wrong... I sinned against God and against you. I don't deserve to be your son. Let me be one of your workers.

17
00:01:47,390 --> 00:01:49,630
Hmm... yes. I'll say that.

18
00:01:50,830 --> 00:01:54,710
Every day, the father stood at the gate and looked down the road.

19
00:01:56,220 --> 00:02:00,130
Is that... is that my boy?!

20
00:02:04,430 --> 00:02:08,330
Dad, I was wrong. I don't deserve to be your son...

21
00:02:08,430 --> 00:02:16,790
Quick! Bring the best robe and put it on him! Put a ring on his finger! We're going to have a feast!

22
00:02:17,470 --> 00:02:18,990
Yes, master!

23
00:02:24,540 --> 00:02:30,220
This son of mine was dead and is alive again! He was lost, and now he is found!

24
00:02:36,830 --> 00:02:42,360
Huh? What's all that noise at home?... What? My brother's back, and Dad's throwing him a party?

25
00:02:46,380 --> 00:02:47,800
Hmph! I'm not going in!

26
00:02:52,490 --> 00:02:57,810
I've worked for you every single day and never disobeyed you. But you never even gave me a little goat!

27
00:03:02,780 --> 00:03:14,290
My son, you are always with me, and everything I have is yours. But your brother was lost and is found. How can we not be glad?

28
00:03:20,180 --> 00:03:28,380
Jesus told this story to show us that God our Father is like this dad. However far you go, he is waiting for you to come home.

29
00:03:29,180 --> 00:03:35,710
If you've done something wrong, say sorry and come back to him. He'll run to give you a big hug!
